cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GeoVersa in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "GeoVersa: Design-Based Residual-Correction Forests for Digital Soil Mapping"
version: 0.5.1
date-released: "2026-10-20"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19380534
url: "https://github.com/HugoMachadoRodrigues/GeoVersa"
repository-code: "https://github.com/HugoMachadoRodrigues/GeoVersa"
license: MIT
type: software
abstract: >-
  GeoVersa implements DB-TARF, a random forest augmented by a cross-fitted,
  out-of-fold-selected residual correction, together with design-based
  conformal prediction intervals whose coverage is estimated from an
  independent probability sample. It is evaluated under the design-based
  paradigm of Wadoux et al. (2021) on their public Amazonian above-ground
  woody biomass benchmark. The package contains source code only and
  redistributes no third-party data.
keywords:
  - digital soil mapping
  - pedometrics
  - design-based inference
  - prediction intervals
  - conformal prediction
  - geostatistics
  - variogram
  - random forest
  - spatial sampling
authors:
  - family-names: Rodrigues
    given-names: Hugo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8070-8126"
